Reject (or decline) malformed export records instead of panicking

Three parser sites panicked on malformed input:
- go1_general unwrapped the record's "ie"/"il"/"in" index for every term
  record, so a term record without one (e.g. a forallE with no "ie") hit
  `Option::unwrap()` on None; it now rejects ("export record is missing
  its index").
- do_proj expected the projection index to fit in u16; a larger "idx"
  now rejects.
- get_uparams unwrapped the level of each declared universe parameter; a
  parameter name no level record mentions now declines (interning it
  would make a later record for the same level a duplicate).
The first was found by a 10-second wasmfuzz smoke run (repro in
suite-repros); the other two by reading the surrounding code.
Regression tests in parser/tests.rs.
Upstream: none (no related issue or PR, checked 2026-11-22).

